Hello! I'm turning forty next month and having a small party, and I hope you =
can come.

We have been clearing out the loft and found a box of old letters from Grandm=
a. Some of them are very funny, and I will bring a few along for you to read.

The book you lent me was wonderful. I stayed up far too late finishing it, an=
d I keep thinking about the ending; we should talk about it next time we meet.

I have started baking bread at the weekends. The first loaf was rather dense,=
 but they are getting better, and the kitchen smells wonderful while it is in=
 the oven.

The dog has been enjoying the cooler mornings. We have started walking the lo=
ng way round the lake, and she always stops to say hello to the ducks by the =
old boathouse.

I took up watercolours again after many years. My first few attempts were mud=
dy, but the evening class has helped, and I am quite pleased with a painting =
of the harbour.

We spent a rainy afternoon at the museum in town. The new gallery about the o=
ld railway was excellent, and the children loved the model trains in the last=
 room.

We had a power cut on Tuesday evening and ended up playing cards by candlelig=
ht. It was rather fun, though the children were less keen once they realised =
the internet was off.

The fox has been visiting the garden again. We see it most evenings just afte=
r dark, trotting along the fence and stopping to look at the house before it =
goes.

The allotment has done well this year. We have more courgettes than we know w=
hat to do with, so do let me know if you would like some when we next see you.

The kittens next door have discovered our garden. They chase leaves across th=
e lawn every afternoon, and I confess I spend far too long watching them from=
 the window.

Thank you again for the recipe. I made the soup on Sunday and everyone went b=
ack for seconds, even my brother, who usually refuses anything with lentils i=
n it.

Dad has been busy in his workshop building a bird table. It is a little lopsi=
ded, but the robins do not seem to mind, and he watches them from the kitchen=
 every morning.

It's on the Saturday after next at our house; let me know if you can make it.

